prompt-chainmail is defensive AI security middleware.

It detects prompt injection, jailbreak-style instruction override, role confusion,
tool-use hijacking, and obfuscated adversarial prompts so applications can block
or flag untrusted input before it reaches an LLM or agent tool layer.

Intended use: protect AI apps and gateways; security research and audit logging.
Not malware: it does not exfiltrate data, persist on hosts, or attack systems.
